      "writtenOn": "2022-05-23T15:21:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This just seems wrong to me.\nThe developer of a VM payload shouldn\u0027t have to worry about leaking things via debug log, because an attacker should not be able to silently acquire those logs.\nThere have definitely been bugs where sensitive information has been accidentally logged and I\u0027m sure there will be more.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 57,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "c4fe6ed00c0120ae0ae5e0450098f77455246b77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d633f98a_aeaee314",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-23T15:35:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does this mean to be temporary (since it\u0027s on master)?  Is there a plan to make this an opt-in option, instead of enabling across the board?\n\nAttack scenario: It\u0027ll be easy for an attacker to run an arbitrary VM given an un-owned APK.  In case there\u0027s any secret in the log, the attacker can reply the RPC requests and retrieve logs via `onPayloadStarted`.  Unless the payload owner is ok with the transparency, without any secret in the log (fine to CompOS I think).",
      "parentUuid": "0b9192bc_9c314bcc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 57,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "c4fe6ed00c0120ae0ae5e0450098f77455246b77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8fe72e82_4c9e702d",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-24T01:24:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is for TM. I\u0027d like to cherry-pick this to tm-dev once it lands here. For U, this will be turned off again, and we will have a means to force enable logging on the guest side if the corresponding debug policy is (securely) provisioned. See go/android-avf-debugging",
      "parentUuid": "d633f98a_aeaee314",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 57,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "c4fe6ed00c0120ae0ae5e0450098f77455246b77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
